# Server-only. Never NEXT_PUBLIC_. The app returns a plan without this key by
# falling back to the keyword parser, so an unset key degrades rather than breaks.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Rate limit store. MemoryStore is dev-only: serverless functions do not share
# memory, so shipping without these means no effective limit at all. Absent in
# production, every policy fails closed.
#
# Two accepted name pairs, checked in this order by lib/server/rateLimitStore.ts.
# Set ONE pair. Upstash's own naming:
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
#
# Or, if the database was provisioned through the Vercel marketplace
# integration, Vercel injects these instead and you set nothing by hand:
#   KV_REST_API_URL
#   KV_REST_API_TOKEN
# KV_REST_API_READ_ONLY_TOKEN is also injected and is deliberately ignored: the
# sliding window counter calls INCR, so a read-only token fails on every write.

# Phase 2 (persistence). Unused in Phase 1, which is stateless.
# DATABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
